From 64dc177d9be0b3914f65f14937912888efe0ae18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 22:02:47 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(sim): plasma through-cut laws - cut order, kerf
 crossing, tip-up
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

#672 step 1 (part of #621's plasma research): sim::verify::plasma judges
a plasma program from a neutral form - the kerf, the cuts in order (each
the torch-on polyline with its contour id, inner/outer and parent outer)
and the rapid into each - so it reads the CL's torch records (#670) and
nothing of the operation's internals:
- cut order (refusal): an inner contour cut after the outer that frees
  its part;
- kerf crossing (warning): a cut within one kerf of an earlier cut's
  centre line - the THC dive the LinuxCNC Plasma Primer §12 warns of;
- tip-up (warning): a rapid across a part already cut free (Tormach
  1300PL manual UM10720 §1.4.2, §4.12.8);
- malformed (refusal): a non-positive or non-finite kerf, a NaN point, a
  cut with no path.
Not yet wired: step 2 reads the plasma op's CL torch records (#670) and
blocks the post on a refusal.

Pinned by plasma_laws (5): each law tripped by one fixture and passed by
another.

Refs #672

